From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 16:41:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gpucc-msm8998: enable runtime PM

gdsc_register() adds every GDSC in a clock controller as a subdomain of the
controller's own power domain, which is how a GPU clock controller can be
placed in the rail its GDSCs depend on. That is only useful if the domain is
released again: without runtime PM it is powered up when the device is
attached and never dropped, voting the rail for the life of the system.

Set use_rpm so qcom_cc_really_probe() drops its reference once probe is
done, leaving the domain held only while one of the GDSCs is on. No
functional change until the DT names a power domain for this controller.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gpucc-msm8998.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gpucc-msm8998.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gpucc-msm8998.c
index 7fce70503141..a37de5bdbaa5 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gpucc-msm8998.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gpucc-msm8998.c
@@ -312,6 +312,13 @@ static const struct qcom_cc_desc gpucc_msm8998_desc = {
 	.num_resets = ARRAY_SIZE(gpucc_msm8998_resets),
 	.gdscs = gpucc_msm8998_gdscs,
 	.num_gdscs = ARRAY_SIZE(gpucc_msm8998_gdscs),
+	/*
+	 * Runtime PM so the VDD_MX domain this controller now sits in is held
+	 * only while one of its GDSCs is on. Without it the domain is powered
+	 * up at attach and never released, which votes MX for the life of the
+	 * system.
+	 */
+	.use_rpm = true,
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id gpucc_msm8998_match_table[] = {
